  "briefing": [
    "Rookery Audio occupies a converted warehouse on Brighton’s North Quay: two recording studios, a small archive, and a late-night radio stream that made its founder famous. On Friday 16 October, the company is hours away from announcing its sale to Vesper Media for eighteen million pounds.",
    "At 22:30, Marcus Vale, 51, Rookery’s founder and CEO, was found dead in Studio B. He had been struck once with a heavy object from the studio. The door was ajar. Nothing obvious was stolen, and the building’s front door was still locked from the inside.",
    "The police believe Marcus died between 22:10 and 22:25. At 23:00, his company’s flagship late-night programme began exactly on time, with host Tom Hargreaves sounding relaxed on air. Tom says he had been live in Studio A all evening.",
    "Marcus’s sister Clare has asked you to look before the police make an arrest. She says her brother was difficult, vain, and very good at hearing the one false note in a room. ‘He was about to sell the thing he built,’ she says. ‘If somebody killed him for it, I want to know what they thought they were saving.’",
    "Everybody who worked late at Rookery is still in Brighton. The sale announcement is paused, the archive is sealed, and the station’s last broadcast is still in the system. Find out what happened before the company’s own story becomes the only one anyone remembers."
  ],
